# Placeholder GUIDs are empty (R6)

The AIC PIM workspace handles many GUID-shaped fields: `agent_uuid`,
`tenant_guid`, `machine_guid`, `enrollment_token_id`, the per-tenant
defaults the server hands agents at enrollment. The
post-2026-05-19 win32 configurator audit found at least four
different "placeholder" GUID values in active use to mean "the
operator has not set this yet":

| Sentinel | Where it was found |
| --- | --- |
| `""` (empty) | Most newer code paths |
| `"0"` | A SQL upsert that defaulted `tenant_guid` |
| `"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"` (zero GUID) | An old import path |
| `"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"` (zero-plus-one) | A test fixture that leaked into a default |
| `"12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"` (sequence GUID) | The Win32 configurator's "Default Tenant" placeholder text |

Five different ways to spell "not configured" produced five
different downstream behaviors: a `WHERE tenant_guid = '0'` query
that matched nothing, an enrollment that sent the zero GUID to the
server and got back a confusing `404 tenant not found`, a Windows
Event Log entry that showed the sequence GUID and looked like real
machine data to the SIEM team. This rule pins the only valid
sentinel — empty — and forbids the magic-GUID variants.

## The rule

> **The sentinel "not yet configured" for any GUID-shaped field
> in this workspace is the empty string. Never `"0"`, never
> `"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"`, never
> `"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"`, never
> `"12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"`, never any other
> placeholder GUID value. Validators check `String::is_empty()`
> (or `Option::None` if the type is `Option<Uuid>`).**

Crates with legacy magic-GUID values still resident on disk
provide a one-shot migration helper of the signature below that
collapses every known magic value to the empty string on first
load (or to `None` if the type is `Option<Uuid>`).

## Forbidden constructs

In every shipping crate in this workspace:

- `const DEFAULT_TENANT_GUID: &str = "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012";`
 or any literal sequence GUID used as a sentinel.
- `const ZERO_GUID: &str = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000";`
 or any literal zero / zero-plus-one GUID used as a sentinel.
 (Real cryptographic uses of the zero GUID — e.g. a documented
 vendor-reserved value in an external protocol — are exempt;
 add a per-site `#[allow]` and a comment.)
- `if guid == "0" { … treat as not set … }` — both the comparison
 string and the practice.
- `Default::default()` on a `Uuid` field that the surrounding
 type later treats as "not set" (this produces the zero GUID
 silently). Use `Option<Uuid>` and `None`, or `String` and
 `""`.
- `let agent = AgentId::new_placeholder()` / any constructor
 that hands back a magic GUID. Either return
 `Result<AgentId, NotConfigured>` or use `Option<AgentId>`.
- `format!("agent={agent_uuid}")` where `agent_uuid` is empty
 and the receiver expects an absent value. Guard with
 `if !agent_uuid.is_empty() { … }` or pass `Option`.

## Required validation pattern

```rust
fn validate_agent_uuid(s: &str) -> Result<(), Validation> {
    if s.is_empty() {
        return Err(Validation::NotConfigured("AGENT_UUID"));
    }
    Uuid::parse_str(s).map_err(|e| Validation::Malformed {
        key: "AGENT_UUID",
        source: e,
    })?;
    Ok(())
}
```

Note that `is_empty()` is the ONLY sentinel check. No
`s == "12345678-…"` branch. No `Uuid::nil() == parsed` branch.
If a legacy magic GUID survives the migration helper (below),
it will fail `Uuid::parse_str(s).is_ok()` for `"0"` and parse
successfully for the four sentinel UUIDs above — at which point
downstream code treats it as a real GUID and reports a clear
"no tenant with that GUID exists" error, which is the correct
behavior post-migration.

## Required one-shot migration helper signature

Every crate that may have legacy magic-GUID values on disk (in
`%PROGRAMDATA%`, HKLM, the legacy `settings.json` import, the
SQL `audit_*` tables) exposes a helper of this shape so a single
upgrade pass cleans them up:

```rust
// pim-app-config/crates/pim-app-config/src/migration.rs
//
// Returns Some(normalized) if `raw` matches a known magic-GUID
// placeholder; returns None if `raw` is already either empty
// or a non-placeholder GUID-shaped value.
pub fn normalize_legacy_guid_sentinel(raw: &str) -> Option<String> {
    const SENTINELS: &[&str] = &[
        "0",
        "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
        "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
        "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012",
    ];
    if SENTINELS.iter().any(|s| s.eq_ignore_ascii_case(raw)) {
        Some(String::new())
    } else {
        None
    }
}
```

Call site (one per crate, in the startup migration path — see
R3):

```rust
for key in ["AGENT_UUID", "DEFAULT_TENANT_GUID", "MACHINE_GUID"] {
    if let Some(raw) = cfg.raw_value(key)? {
        if let Some(normalized) = normalize_legacy_guid_sentinel(&raw) {
            tracing::info!(%key, %raw, "collapsing legacy magic-GUID placeholder to empty");
            cfg.set_value(key, &normalized)?;
        }
    }
}
```

`set_value` enforces R2 (manifest gate), so this also catches
the case where the legacy file held the magic GUID under a key
the new manifest no longer declares.

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation** (today, in a hypothetical SQL upsert path):

```rust
let tenant = req.tenant_guid.unwrap_or_else(|| "0".to_string());
sqlx::query("INSERT INTO offline_agents (id, tenant_guid) VALUES ($1, $2)")
    .bind(agent.id())
    .bind(&tenant)
    .execute(&mut tx).await?;
```

A subsequent query `WHERE tenant_guid = ?` with the operator's
real tenant GUID misses the inserted row. A migration query
trying to "fix" the zero GUIDs later cannot tell the legitimate
"not yet enrolled" rows from the legitimate "zero is a real
GUID in some other system" rows.

**Fix** (typed: `Option<Uuid>` end-to-end; empty string when
serialized; explicit `NULL` in SQL):

```rust
let tenant: Option<Uuid> = req.tenant_guid; // None if operator did not provide
sqlx::query("INSERT INTO offline_agents (id, tenant_guid) VALUES ($1, $2)")
    .bind(agent.id())
    .bind(tenant)  // sqlx binds None as NULL
    .execute(&mut tx).await?;
```

The audit log and the configurator UI render `tenant_guid` as
empty when the column is `NULL`; the SQL `WHERE tenant_guid = ?`
no longer false-positively matches a placeholder.

## Configurator GUI surfacing rule

The four configurator GUIs render any `operator_must_set` GUID
field as empty (placeholder text in the input control, not in
the value). The first-run banner from R5 names the empty fields.
If an operator types `"0"` or `"00000000-…"` and clicks Save, the
manifest validator (R2) rejects the value with
`InvalidValue { key, reason: "placeholder GUID is not a valid
configured value; leave empty if not yet set" }`. The dialog
keeps the field highlighted with the reason in the status pane.

